# tpu-jax-inf2-2b — authoritative configuration.
#
# The directory name is documentation; this file decides. Never copy a slot value
# out of the directory name into a CLI flag (NAMING.md, "The name is a claim").
#
# STATUS: THE SERVING PATH IS NOT WIRED YET. Created 2026-08-28 by forking
# `tpu-pytorch-inf2-2b` for its Neuron provisioning and bringing the JAX engine
# (`ports/gemma4/`, `jax_engine.py`, `jax_openai_server.py`) across from
# `gpu-jax-g5g-2b`. `server.py` still deploys the inherited vLLM-Neuron Docker
# container; replacing that with a systemd JAX unit is the open work.
#
# WHY THIS RIG IS WORTH BUILDING, stated from measurements that already exist in
# `tpu-pytorch-inf2-2b/benchmarks/runs/`:
#
#   * 2026-08-02 parity: the engine is TOKEN-EXACT on Neuron at ~14 tok/s with
#     NEURON_RUN_TRIVIAL_COMPUTATION_ON_CPU **off**, for the unquantized export
#     at --quant-mode fp16 --kv-cache-dtype bf16.
#   * The silent-garbage fault lives in the w4a16 + int8-KV configuration, NOT
#     in the engine. This rig deliberately serves the DENSE REFERENCE build, so
#     it sits inside the configuration parity proved correct.
#   * inf2.xlarge is $0.1417/hr spot average (7-day, us-east-1, 2026-08-28) --
#     about a third of g5g.2xlarge, for a comparable measured decode rate.
#
# WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED, per the same reports: parity drove the engine
# IN-PROCESS, not through HTTP; it used 4 prompts / 24 tokens / batch 1 / greedy
# / UNWINDOWED KV, while the server runs windowed. Closing that gap is the whole
# point of this rig. Do not quote ~14 tok/s as this rig's result.

# --- Model -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The dense reference release -- chosen because it is the configuration that
# passed parity on Neuron, not for convenience. No encoding slot in the name.
MODEL_NAME=google/gemma-4-E2B-it
QUANT_MODE=fp16
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=bf16

# --- Hardware ----------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SIZE LADDER IS NOT WHAT THE SUFFIX SUGGESTS. Verified against
# describe_instance_types 2026-08-28 (Inferentia reports under
# `InferenceAcceleratorInfo`; `AcceleratorInfo` comes back EMPTY and reads as
# "no accelerator"):
#
#   size            chips  cores  accel MiB  GiB/core  vCPU  host GiB   $/hr spot
#   inf2.xlarge         1      2     32,768      16.0     4        16     0.1417
#   inf2.8xlarge        1      2     32,768      16.0    32       128     0.5552
#   inf2.24xlarge       6     12    196,608      16.0    96       384     2.2670
#   inf2.48xlarge      12     24    393,216      16.0   192       768     8.3988
#
# Two consequences, and both cost money if missed:
#
#   * inf2.xlarge and inf2.8xlarge CARRY THE SAME ACCELERATOR. 8xlarge is ~4x
#     the spot price for zero extra compute and zero extra accelerator memory.
#     The only thing it buys is host RAM.
#   * ACCELERATOR MEMORY IS PER CORE, NOT A POOL -- 16 GiB on every size in the
#     table, including the 12-chip 48xlarge. A single-device engine gets 16 GiB
#     no matter what you pay. This is why chip count is NOT in the rig name;
#     NAMING.md puts it here instead, and here is where it stays.
#
# So the default is the SMALLEST size, on purpose, and the reason to move up is
# host RAM alone -- see the swapfile note below.
INSTANCE_TYPE=inf2.xlarge
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=1
# MEASURED (HARDWARE.md): hbm_limit_bytes = 17,179,869,184 = 16 GiB PER
# NeuronCore, reported identically whether one core or two is visible. 32 GB is
# 16 GiB x 2 cores, NOT a pool -- a single-device engine gets 16 GiB.
# NEURON_RT_NUM_CORES=1 therefore withholds a DEVICE, not memory.

# --- Neuron-specific, and both of these are load-bearing ----------------------
# MEASURED 2026-08-02: the workaround is what costs 65x (2700x on the older
# stack). Parity says the engine does not need it for THIS checkpoint and dtype
# combination, so it stays off and correctness is asserted, not assumed.
NEURON_RUN_TRIVIAL_COMPUTATION_ON_CPU=0
# MEASURED 2026-08-02: setting this is a HARD CRASH on jax 0.9.2 for Neuron --
# the service crash-loops before the model loads with
#   RET_CHECK failure: proto.has_host_program_shape()
# `ports/gemma4/backend.py` declares persistent_compilation_cache=False for
# Neuron and the capability table was right. Leave this EMPTY.
JAX_COMPILATION_CACHE_DIR=

# --- Host RAM ----------------------------------------------------------------
# inf2.xlarge has EXACTLY 16 GiB and the one-time load peaks ~14.5 GB, so it
# needs a swapfile and the threshold is INCLUSIVE at 16 -- the same boundary the
# `gpu-jax` line settled on after `< 16` skipped the one size that needed it.
# `_needs_swap()` returns True for inf2.xlarge and False for everything above.
#
# If load-time host pressure ever proves unfixable, inf2.8xlarge's 128 GiB is
# the remedy -- and it is the ONLY thing that instance buys. Decide that on a
# measurement, not on the size suffix.

# --- Serving -----------------------------------------------------------------
MAX_MODEL_LEN=4096
MAX_NUM_SEQS=1
JAX_PORT=8000
SERVICE_NAME=jax-inf2
HF_SECRET_ID=vllm/hf-token
